1	2026 Meher Season Planting Advisory	High probability of normal rainfall. Farmers should prioritize early land preparation.	Use improved seed varieties and ensure proper drainage.	2026-02-17	Seasonal	Slightly above average	Mild during germination	Waterlogging in valley areas	advisory_media/Screenshot_2026-02-16_185047.png	2026-02-17 20:09:19.356835+00	2026 Meher Season Planting Advisory	የ2026 የመኸር ወቅት የዝግጅት ምክ	ናይ 2026 ወቕቲ መከር ምኽሪ	Gorsa Qonnaa Arfaasaa 2026	High probability of normal rainfall. Farmers should prioritize early land preparation.	መደበኛ የዝናብ ስርጭት ስለሚጠበቅ ገበሬዎች ቀድመው መሬት ማዘጋጀት አለባቸው።	ንቡር ዝናብ ስለ ዝጽበ፡ ሓረስቶት ቀዲሞም መሬት ከዳልዉ ይግባእ።	Roobni idilee waan eegamuuf qonnaan bultoonni lafa qopheessuu qabu.	Use improved seed varieties and ensure proper drainage.	የተሻሻሉ የዘር ዝርያዎችን ይጠቀሙ እና የውሃ ፍሳሽን ያረጋግጡ።	ዝተመሓየሹ ዓሌት ዘርኢ ተጠቐሙ፡ ውሕጅ ማይ ድማ ኣረጋግጹ።	Sanyii filatamaa fayyadamaa, bishaan dhangala'aa mirkaneessaa.	Waterlogging in valley areas	በሸለቆማ አካባቢዎች የውሃ መቋጠር	ኣብ ስንጭሮታት ምእካብ ማይ	Sulula keessatti dhangala'aa bishaanie	Slightly above average	ከመደበኛው መጠነኛ ከፍ ያለ	ካብ ንቡር ቁሩብ ዝለዓለ	Giddu-galeessa ol-xiqqoo	Mild during germination	ለብቀላ ወቅት ተስማሚ ሙቀት	ንምብቃይ ዝጥዕም ሙቀት	Yeroo biqilaaf mijaawaa	\N	\N
2	2026 Belg Season Agro-Climate Advisory	The Belg (short rains) season is forecast to bring near-normal to slightly below-normal rainfall across the central and eastern wheat clusters. Farmers are advised to prepare land early and prioritise short-maturing, drought-tolerant wheat varieties.	Plant early with certified seed of short-maturing varieties, apply moisture-conserving tillage, and scout for stripe rust from tillering onward.	2026-07-20	Seasonal	Near-normal to slightly below-normal rainfall (February-May), with a delayed onset in eastern clusters.	Warmer-than-average daytime temperatures expected, increasing crop water demand.	Moisture stress during establishment; elevated risk of stripe rust in cooler highland pockets during moist spells.		2026-07-20 17:55:13.690605+00	2026 Belg Season Agro-Climate Advisory	\N	\N	\N	The Belg (short rains) season is forecast to bring near-normal to slightly below-normal rainfall across the central and eastern wheat clusters. Farmers are advised to prepare land early and prioritise short-maturing, drought-tolerant wheat varieties.	\N	\N	\N	Plant early with certified seed of short-maturing varieties, apply moisture-conserving tillage, and scout for stripe rust from tillering onward.	\N	\N	\N	Moisture stress during establishment; elevated risk of stripe rust in cooler highland pockets during moist spells.	\N	\N	\N	Near-normal to slightly below-normal rainfall (February-May), with a delayed onset in eastern clusters.	\N	\N	\N	Warmer-than-average daytime temperatures expected, increasing crop water demand.	\N	\N	\N		1
3	Kiremt 2026 Rust Alert and Crop Management	Favourable moist conditions during the main Kiremt season raise the risk of wheat rust epidemics. Growers should monitor fields and be ready to apply fungicides on susceptible varieties.	Scout weekly, prioritise flag-leaf protection, ensure field drainage, and use resistant varieties where available.	2026-07-20	Monthly	Above-normal rainfall likely during July-August across highland wheat clusters.	Cool, moist conditions favourable for fungal disease development.	High risk of stem and stripe rust; waterlogging in poorly drained soils.		2026-07-20 17:55:14.265752+00	Kiremt 2026 Rust Alert and Crop Management	\N	\N	\N	Favourable moist conditions during the main Kiremt season raise the risk of wheat rust epidemics. Growers should monitor fields and be ready to apply fungicides on susceptible varieties.	\N	\N	\N	Scout weekly, prioritise flag-leaf protection, ensure field drainage, and use resistant varieties where available.	\N	\N	\N	High risk of stem and stripe rust; waterlogging in poorly drained soils.	\N	\N	\N	Above-normal rainfall likely during July-August across highland wheat clusters.	\N	\N	\N	Cool, moist conditions favourable for fungal disease development.	\N	\N	\N		1
